doc:sec-8ab-ss-4 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "8AB(4) Power of Judge to order that jurisdiction in a matter be" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(4) Where an order has been made under either of the last two preceding subsections in relation to a matter:  (a) the jurisdiction of the Court in that matter shall, subject to the Rules of Court, be exercised by not less than three Judges sitting together in Court; and  (c) the Court may give such directions as it thinks proper as to the procedure to be followed in the further conduct of the proceedings, including, in a case where evidence" ;
    cof:pageNumber "13"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-8ac a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "8AC Manner in which question to be decided where jurisdiction"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-8ac ;
    values:originalText "exercised by 3 or more Judges  If three or more Judges sitting together in accordance with section 8AAA, 8AA or 8AB are divided in opinion as to the decision to be given on any question, the question shall be decided according to the opinion of the majority, if there is a majority, but if the Judges are equally divided in opinion:  (a) in a case where a judgment of the Master is called in question—the judgment shall be affirmed; and  (b) in any other case:  (i) where a Judge or Judges appointed under subsection 7(1) is or are sitting—the opinion of that Judge or of the senior of them, as the case may be, prevails; or  (ii) where no such Judge is sitting—the opinion of the senior additional Judge sitting prevails." ;
    skos:definition "exercised by 3 or more Judges  If three or more Judges sitting together in accordance with section 8AAA, 8AA or 8AB are divided in opinion as to the decision to be given on any question, the question shall be decided according to the opinion of the majority, if there is a majority, but if the Judges are equally divided in opinion:  (a) in a case where a judgment of the Master is called in question—the judgment shall be affirmed; and  (b) in any other case:  (i) where a Judge or Judges appointed under subsection 7(1) is or are sitting—the opinion of that Judge or of the senior of them, as the case may be, prevails; or  (ii) where no such Judge is sitting—the opinion of the senior additional Judge sitting prevails."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a09701c65871f0f18c39f491418892f88e50e40ae14aa32367c89d6551cac98c" ;
    cof:pageNumber "14"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Judges' decision on a question is decided according to the majority opinion, with certain exceptions." ;
