concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-21 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "21 Equities appearing incidentally"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-21 ;
    values:originalText "The Supreme Court or the Judge shall take notice of all equitable estates, titles and rights, and all equitable duties and liabilities appearing incidentally in the course of any cause or matter, in the same manner in which the English Court of Chancery would, immediately before the commencement of the Judicature Act, have taken notice of those matters in any suit or proceeding properly instituted therein.   Constitution and Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court  Part II  Section 22  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933" ;
    skos:definition "The Supreme Court or the Judge shall take notice of all equitable estates, titles and rights, and all equitable duties and liabilities appearing incidentally in the course of any cause or matter, in the same manner in which the English Court of Chancery would, immediately before the commencement of the Judicature Act, have taken notice of those matters in any suit or proceeding properly instituted therein.   Constitution and Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court  Part II  Section 22  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "17abe6662c204f8799232271598fc9a3291f7c2ce4ed29028be2c3bfcac47a65" ;
    cof:pageNumber "20"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Notice of equitable estates and rights appearing incidentally in court proceedings." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
