doc:sec-26-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "26(3) Mandamus, injunctions and receivers" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If, whether before, or at, or after the hearing of any cause or matter, an application is made for an injunction to prevent any threatened or apprehended waste or trespass, the injunction may be granted, if the Court thinks fit, whether the person against whom the injunction is sought is or is not in possession under any claim of title or otherwise, or (if out of possession) does or does not claim a right to do the act sought to be restrained under any colour of title, and whether the estates claimed by both or by either of the parties are legal or equitable.   Constitution and Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court  Part II  Section 27  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-27 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "27 Practice and procedure"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-27 ;
    values:originalText "Where no provision in relation to a matter of practice and procedure of the Supreme Court is contained in this or any other Act, an Ordinance, an enactment or Rules of Court, that matter shall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the High Court in similar matters and, if that practice and procedure is not applicable, that matter shall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the Supreme Court of New South Wales." ;
    skos:definition "Where no provision in relation to a matter of practice and procedure of the Supreme Court is contained in this or any other Act, an Ordinance, an enactment or Rules of Court, that matter shall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the High Court in similar matters and, if that practice and procedure is not applicable, that matter shall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the Supreme Court of New South Wales."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "06c2f05a97427e164fc6c35b9b6383e206ae8e23580c01b7ba3c59c062161b7b" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Governs practice and procedure of Supreme Court by High Court or Supreme Court of New South Wales" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.23" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-27-norm .
