doc:sec-27 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "27 Practice and procedure" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Where no provision in relation to a matter of practice and procedure of the Supreme Court is contained in this or any other Act, an Ordinance, an enactment or Rules of Court, that matter shall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the High Court in similar matters and, if that practice and procedure is not applicable, that matter shall be governed, as nearly as may be, by the practice and procedure of the Supreme Court of New South Wales." ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-28 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "28 Rules of Court"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-28 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Judges appointed under subsection (1) of section 7 or any two of those Judges may make Rules of Court, not inconsistent with this or any other Act, with regulations under this or any other Act or with any Ordinance:  (a) for regulating and prescribing:  (i) the practice and procedure, including the method of pleading, to be followed in the Supreme Court and in the offices of the Court; and  (ii) all matters and things incidental to or relating to any such practice and procedure or necessary or convenient to be prescribed for the conduct of any business of the Court;  (b) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by any law of the Commonwealth or of the Territory that makes provision for the incorporation of, and otherwise in relation to, companies, required or permitted to be prescribed by regulation under that law;  (c) for prescribing the qualifications for the admission of persons to practise as barristers and solicitors of the Supreme Court; and  (d) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by this Act or by any Ordinance or enactment, required or permitted to be prescribed by Rules of Court.  (2) In particular the Rules of Court may provide:  (a) for the places of sitting of the Court;" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Judges appointed under subsection (1) of section 7 or any two of those Judges may make Rules of Court, not inconsistent with this or any other Act, with regulations under this or any other Act or with any Ordinance:  (a) for regulating and prescribing:  (i) the practice and procedure, including the method of pleading, to be followed in the Supreme Court and in the offices of the Court; and  (ii) all matters and things incidental to or relating to any such practice and procedure or necessary or convenient to be prescribed for the conduct of any business of the Court;  (b) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by any law of the Commonwealth or of the Territory that makes provision for the incorporation of, and otherwise in relation to, companies, required or permitted to be prescribed by regulation under that law;  (c) for prescribing the qualifications for the admission of persons to practise as barristers and solicitors of the Supreme Court; and  (d) for prescribing any matter or thing that is, by this Act or by any Ordinance or enactment, required or permitted to be prescribed by Rules of Court.  (2) In particular the Rules of Court may provide:  (a) for the places of sitting of the Court;"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4090702bbec3d23ce230db38bc3c4b748779c9e58f0e8e7aab1c0f488a0b8a1f" ;
    cof:pageNumber "23"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-28-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-28-ss-2 ;
