concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-29 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "29 Regulations relating to fees"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-29 ;
    values:originalText "The Governor-General may make regulations:  (a) prescribing the fees or other payments to be paid to officers of the Court in respect of proceedings in the Court, or of the service or execution of the process of the Court by officers of the Court; and  (b) making provision, not inconsistent with this Act, necessary or convenient to be made for and in relation to the payment or remission of any such fees or other payments.   The Master  Part III  Section 30  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933" ;
    skos:definition "The Governor-General may make regulations:  (a) prescribing the fees or other payments to be paid to officers of the Court in respect of proceedings in the Court, or of the service or execution of the process of the Court by officers of the Court; and  (b) making provision, not inconsistent with this Act, necessary or convenient to be made for and in relation to the payment or remission of any such fees or other payments.   The Master  Part III  Section 30  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7732bdffbefb77abe2ec77a0585e5f8e873c4103422c19239a094216d02d83a3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "24"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Governor-General may make regulations regarding fees and payments." ;
