concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-32 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "32 Appointment of Master"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-32 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Master shall be appointed by the Governor-General.  (2) A person shall not be appointed as the Master unless the person has been enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court or of the Supreme Court of a State or Territory for not less than 5 years.  (3) A person who has attained 65 years of age shall not be appointed as the Master." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Master shall be appointed by the Governor-General.  (2) A person shall not be appointed as the Master unless the person has been enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court or of the Supreme Court of a State or Territory for not less than 5 years.  (3) A person who has attained 65 years of age shall not be appointed as the Master."@en ;
