concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-45 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "45 Matter heard at one place may be further dealt with at another"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-45 ;
    values:originalText "place  When any cause or matter has been heard at a sitting of the Supreme Court held at any place the Court may pronounce judgment or give further hearing or consideration to the cause or matter at a sitting of the Court held at another place, being a place at which the Court is empowered to sit." ;
    skos:definition "place  When any cause or matter has been heard at a sitting of the Supreme Court held at any place the Court may pronounce judgment or give further hearing or consideration to the cause or matter at a sitting of the Court held at another place, being a place at which the Court is empowered to sit."@en ;
