doc:sec-49 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "49 Date of process" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "All writs and process issued from the Supreme Court shall be dated as of the day on which they are issued." ;
    cof:pageNumber "36"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-50 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "50 Oaths and affirmations"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-50 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to any Ordinance or to Rules of Court, the forms of oath used in proceedings in the Supreme Court shall be the same, as nearly as may be, as those which are used in the Supreme Court of the State of New South Wales.  (2) Subject to any Ordinance or to Rules of Court, a person who, by or under a law of the State of New South Wales, is entitled to make an affirmation instead of taking an oath may do so in a cause or matter in the Supreme Court.  (3) The form of affirmation shall, subject to any Ordinance or to Rules of Court, be in accordance with the law of that State.   Miscellaneous  Part VII  Section 53  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to any Ordinance or to Rules of Court, the forms of oath used in proceedings in the Supreme Court shall be the same, as nearly as may be, as those which are used in the Supreme Court of the State of New South Wales.  (2) Subject to any Ordinance or to Rules of Court, a person who, by or under a law of the State of New South Wales, is entitled to make an affirmation instead of taking an oath may do so in a cause or matter in the Supreme Court.  (3) The form of affirmation shall, subject to any Ordinance or to Rules of Court, be in accordance with the law of that State.   Miscellaneous  Part VII  Section 53  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933"@en ;
