concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-58 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "58 Liability and protection of receivers and managers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-58 ;
    values:originalText "A receiver or manager of any property appointed by the Supreme Court may, without the previous leave of the Court, be sued in respect of any act or transaction of his in carrying on the business connected with the property. 59  Action by or against Sheriff etc.  When the Sheriff or a Deputy Sheriff is a party to a cause in the Supreme Court, all writs, summonses, orders, warrants, precepts, process and commands in the cause which should in the ordinary course be directed to him shall be directed to such disinterested person as the Court or the Judge appoints; and the person so appointed may execute and return them.   Endnotes  Endnote 1—Legislation history  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933  Endnotes  Endnote 1—Legislation history This endnote sets out details of the legislation history of the Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933.  Act Number and year Assent Commencement Application, saving and transitional provisions Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933 34, 1933" ;
    skos:definition "A receiver or manager of any property appointed by the Supreme Court may, without the previous leave of the Court, be sued in respect of any act or transaction of his in carrying on the business connected with the property. 59  Action by or against Sheriff etc.  When the Sheriff or a Deputy Sheriff is a party to a cause in the Supreme Court, all writs, summonses, orders, warrants, precepts, process and commands in the cause which should in the ordinary course be directed to him shall be directed to such disinterested person as the Court or the Judge appoints; and the person so appointed may execute and return them.   Endnotes  Endnote 1—Legislation history  Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933  Endnotes  Endnote 1—Legislation history This endnote sets out details of the legislation history of the Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933.  Act Number and year Assent Commencement Application, saving and transitional provisions Australian Capital Territory Supreme Court Act 1933 34, 1933"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1f8fee4219dac5c5c2853d01965c5d62a220f27d652ca44a8bc5a670ecb831bb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "40"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "A receiver or manager may be sued without previous leave of the Court." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf> ;
    dc:source "australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933.pdf, p.40" ;
    cml:asserts concept:australian-capital-territory-supreme-court-act-1933-sec-58-norm .
